    "sections": {
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "description": "<p>A small utility plugin to help copy WooCommerce orders from one site to another with just a couple of clicks.</p>\n<h3>Development</h3>\n<p>This plugin is built using WordPress&#8217;s <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/block-editor/reference-guides/packages/packages-scripts/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">JS Tooling</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/squizlabs/PHP_CodeSniffer\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">PHP_CodeSniffer</a>, and <a href=\"https://phpstan.org/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">PHPStan</a>.  it strictly adheres to WordPress&#8217;s <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/coding-standards/wordpress-coding-standards/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">PHP Coding Standards</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/coding-standards/javascript/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">JavaScript Coding Standards</a>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Clone the repository.</li>\n<li>Run <code>composer install</code> to install dependencies.</li>\n<li>Run <code>yarn install</code> to install JavaScript dependencies.</li>\n<li>Run <code>yarn dev</code> to start the development server.</li>\n<li>Run <code>yarn test</code> to run the tests.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Source</h3>\n<p>https://github.com/dream-encode/copy-paste-order-for-woocommerce</p>\n"
    },
